{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/569799-body-slams-head-butts-and-tackles","id":569799,"title":"Body Slams, Head Butts, and Tackles","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-26T17:24:56-07:00","id":569799,"title":"Body Slams, Head Butts, and Tackles","content":"So, as a general question, do V20 and M20 also have these maneuvers listed, and if so, does the head butt say that it's executed like a body slam but resemble, in text and mechanics, a tackle instead, as in W20?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T02:33:14-07:00","id":572459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mage 20</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Tackle:</b> Employing a mix of weight and momentum,<br /> the attacker throws herself into her opponent. This sort of<br /> thing can hurt both parties, but it\u2019s an effective way to stop a<br /> fleeing enemy. A tackle requires at least two yards of distance to achieve<br /> effective momentum. Each combatant must make a successful<br /> Dexterity + Athletics roll (difficulty 6 for the attacker, difficulty<br /> 6 + the attacker\u2019s successes for the target), or else wind up<br /> sprawled on the ground afterward.<br /> A would-be tackler who botches either trips and falls<br /> (inflicting one die of damage upon herself for every yard she<br /> ran); slams into something else (inflicting that damage plus her<br /> Strength damage upon herself); or crashes into her target and<br /> bounces off (suffering the opponent\u2019s Stamina in damage and<br /> leaving the target himself unharmed).<br /> For the most part, tackle damage is bashing, not lethal. A<br /> person crushed beneath the weight of a flying cyborg, however<br /> \u2013 or hit by someone who\u2019s suddenly amped her mass with Life<br /> or her momentum with Forces \u2013 is liable to need a hospital,<br /> stat; in game terms, this tactic inflicts lethal damage instead.<br /> Do we really need to point out that a fragile human mage who<br /> flings herself into a cyborg or mass-enhanced body is liable to<br /> suffer that kind of damage herself\u2026?<br /> <br /> Roll: Dexterity + Brawl Difficulty: 7<br /> Damage: Strength/B or L Actions: 1<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Body Slam:</b> Lifting his opponent up over his head, a<br /> strong fighter can use brute strength and momentum to burst<br /> various important innards. <br /> This maneuver requires a successful grappling attack. If<br /> the enemy can\u2019t break free within that turn, the brawler can<br /> use his next action to slam his foe into the nearest and most<br /> painful surface. The impact typically inflicts bashing damage;<br /> if the surface happens to be sharp, spiked, or incredibly hot,<br /> however, such injuries might be lethal instead.<br /> <br /> Roll: Dexterity + Brawl/B or L Difficulty: 6<br /> Damage: Strength +2 Actions: 2<br /> <br /> <b>Head Butt:</b> In a close-clinch situation, the attacker<br /> can smash her head into the face or stomach of an opponent.<br /> Obviously, this move works only when both antagonists are within<br /> head\u2019s reach of one another \u2013 the attack\u2019s main benefit comes<br /> from surprise, backed up by a sudden thick skull in the teeth.<br /> Unless the attacker has a horned head, spiked helmet, steel<br /> skull, or other lethal implement, the head butt inflicts bashing<br /> damage. If the target soaks all of that damage, however, then<br /> the attacker is stunned for one turn. Anyone stupid enough to<br /> head butt a cyborg or other unyielding opponent suffers the<br /> damage she would have inflicted and gets stunned for a turn<br /> as well. (For rules about being stunned, see<br /> Blinded, Knocked Down, Immobilized, or Stunned, above.)<br /> <br /> Roll: Dexterity + Brawl Difficulty: 6<br /> Damage: Strength +1/B Actions: 1</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>V20 Says</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Tackle:</b> The attacker rushes her opponent, tack-<br /> ling him to the ground. The attack roll is at +1 dif-<br /> ficulty, and the maneuver inflicts Strength +1 damage.<br /> Additionally, both combatants must roll Dexterity<br /> + Athletics (difficulty 7) or suffer a knockdown (see<br /> \u201cManeuver Complications,\u201d p. 279). Even if the tar-<br /> get\u2019s Athletics roll succeeds, he is unbalanced, suffer-<br /> ing +1 difficulty to his actions for the next turn.<br /> <br /> Traits: Strength + Brawl Difficulty: +1</div> </div> </div> </div>The Head Butt and the Body Slam do not exist in Vampire. This is one of those reasons why I tend to skip reading the rules section in the WW books and just wing stuff like manoeuvres :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T05:43:04-07:00","id":572534,"title":"","content":"So the M20 head butt is an actual head butt, while the W20 headbutt is really more of a ram that doesn't know what the text of the body slam maneuver says...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T06:57:49-07:00","id":572604,"title":"","content":"The manouver rules in Mage are quite elaborate. There is 11 pages of different tricks for the PC's to pull off.<br /> I find it ironic that its combat is more detailed and complex then Werewolf's.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T07:39:05-07:00","id":572626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/569799-body-slams-head-butts-and-tackles?p=572604#post572604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The manouver rules in Mage are quite elaborate. There is 11 pages of different tricks for the PC's to pull off.<br /> I find it ironic that its combat is more detailed and complex then Werewolf's.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having Gifts, claws, fangs, and superhuman physical prowess of every kind can sort of simplify things, I guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T04:58:25-07:00","id":573736,"title":"","content":"Tssss. I feel that Werwolf thrives on quality cinematic combat and that you should motivate the players to pull off crazy shit and look like the coolest warriors of all. This is the reason why i encourage people to be experimental with what they can do and only give them manouvers as inspiration and examples of what can be pulled off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T16:34:31-07:00","id":585350,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I just cheat and rely on simple Dexterity + Brawl rolls, perhaps with a bonus if the character attempts something really clever and fitting. The other stuff just bogs stuff down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}